  "note": "Operator-signed lifecycle substrate for verified_levers when intel.json lacks policy_lifecycle. Every URL is drawn from data/policy/intel.json sources on main. One stage per cited document. A seed row's event_date is the cited document's own date, at the precision the source actually supports. Optional date_precision is day (default), month, or undated. Day when the URL or the intel.json fact that names the document states a calendar day. Month when only a month is attested: event_date is the first of that month, ordering uses that first, and the 45-day stall arithmetic uses the last day of the month so a gap is never overstated. Undated when the cited document attests the stage but carries no date: event_date is null, the stage still counts as reached, the date slot reads 'date not published', the row never sets the newest-dated-stage chip, and it never anchors stall arithmetic. When an item's newest reached stage is undated the item is not called stalled. Never a multi-stage ladder from a single URL.",
